# Style rules

## Languages

- Agent and UI server: TypeScript on Node 22, run with tsx, ES modules. No runtime dependencies in `agent/package.json`; devDependencies are tsx, typescript and vitest at pinned versions.
- Zetaris gateway: Python 3.12 in the repo-root `.venv`, FastAPI + JayDeBeApi + JPype1 (`gateway/requirements.txt`).
- UI: plain HTML, CSS and ES modules in `ui/`, no build step, live updates over SSE from `/api/events`.

## Code

- Small, focused modules matching the layout in `AGENTS.md`. Deterministic logic (verifiers, policy, statements, GTIN checks) stays free of model calls so it can be unit-tested.
- Model output is parsed against a JSON schema; invalid output is retried once, then a deterministic fallback step is taken and labelled "fallback step".
- Every claim shown to the officer lists one or more evidence ids from `agent/src/evidence/store.ts`.
- Ops JSON files are written atomically (temp file, then rename).
- Comments explain why, not what changed.

## Tests

- TypeScript: vitest, files in `agent/test/*.test.ts`; run `cd agent && npm test`.
- Python: pytest in `gateway/tests/`.
- A task is done when its listed tests pass. Do not weaken or skip a test to make it pass.

## Commits

- Stage explicit paths only. Cursor Agent commits use the message `Cn: <task> (Cursor Agent)`.
- Plain commit messages: no co-author lines and no other trailers.
- Public text (README, docs, code comments, commit messages) names no development tool other than Cursor.
